/-!
# Reductions for the faithful FF exclusions on p.1152

The offender-generated restriction establishes G = J(G,V) without imposing
that equality on an arbitrary module. Kernel comparison identifies the actual
faithful section image, and the central-quotient construction turns the
B.5.1 supplement and natural-module outputs into a nonsplit extension.

The source exclusions and the SL2 exceptional identification remain to be
assembled. Their upstream obligations are the complete B.4.2 alternatives
(including exact ratios and offender clauses), the complete B.5.1 conclusions
under its faithful, finite, two-core, generation and generalized-Fitting
hypotheses, and the actual E.2.2 model comparisons for central covers and
induced diagram automorphisms. In particular B.5.1 cannot be applied to an
exchanged product as if its generalized Fitting subgroup were quasisimple.

No theorem in this module yet excludes FF-modules for those model families.
The parent source-module case split remains independent of this development.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), 15.3.65,
printed p.1152; F.9.18(6), pp.325--326; B.4.2, pp.86--87; B.5.1, pp.99--100.
-/
